WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.120
Conversation starters is a great tool for getting deeper and more interesting information

00:05.120 --> 00:06.720
when you're out in the field.

00:06.720 --> 00:11.440
This can be especially helpful when you're dealing with cultures other than your own.

00:11.440 --> 00:16.920
As an example, when we were recently doing a project in Mexico to design savings programs,

00:16.920 --> 00:21.920
we actually started with some concepts to get people to react and start to talk to us

00:21.920 --> 00:25.520
in ways that they might not otherwise if we had just asked simple questions.

00:25.520 --> 00:29.720
So what you see here are examples of a couple different things we created.

00:29.720 --> 00:33.240
Around the question of how people might want to access their money.

00:33.240 --> 00:37.640
We put money in a brick, we put money in a pillow, we put money in an envelope.

00:37.640 --> 00:41.680
None of these are actually the concepts we intend to design, but what they do is create

00:41.680 --> 00:46.040
a great way for people to react and give us more information around how they feel or

00:46.040 --> 00:49.960
how they think about something rather than just simply asking a basic question.

